<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>Differential Equations Review</title>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>The differential equation
  <md>y'' = -16y</md>
  describes the height of an object suspended by a spring.  Which of
  the following functions are solutions of this equation?</p>
        <p><m>\bullet\, y=-16\sin(t)</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p><m>\bullet\, y=-16\sin(4t)</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p><m>\bullet\, y=-16\cos(4t)</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>The velocity of a falling object is described by the
  differential equation
  <md>
  v' = 9.8 - 2v.
  </md>
  Which of the following functions are solutions of this equation?</p>
        <p><m>\bullet\, v = 9.8t - t^2</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p><m>\bullet\, v = 4.9 + 3e^{-2t}</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p><m>\bullet\, v = 4.9</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>For what velocities does the velocity increase?  For what velocities
  does the velocity decrease?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>Sketch a slope field for this differential equation.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Identify any equilibrium solutions and determine whether they are
  stable or unstable.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>What does this equilibrium solution mean in terms of the falling
  object?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that <m>v</m> is measured in meters per second and <m>t</m> is measured in
  seconds.  Let's develop a numerical approximation of the solution
  that has an 
  initial value of <m>v(0) = 0</m>.  What is the rate of change <m>dv/dt</m> at
  this time?  What are the units on this rate of change?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>If we take time steps of <m>\Delta t = 0.5</m> seconds, by approximately
  how much does the velocity change from <m>t=0</m> to <m>t=0.1</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>What is the estimate velocity when <m>t=0.1</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Repeat this process to continue estimating the velocity (remember
  that this is called Euler's method and pronounced ``Oiler's
  method'')</p>
        <p>\begin{tabular}{c|c|c|c}
      <m>t</m> &amp;<m>v</m> &amp; <m>dv/dt</m> &amp; <m>\Delta v</m> 
      \hline
      0 &amp; 0 &amp; \bm\bm &amp; \bm\bm 
      \bm0.1 &amp;&amp;&amp;
      \bm0.2 &amp;\bm\bm\bm&amp;\bm\bm&amp;\bm\bm
      \bm0.3 &amp;\bm\bm&amp;\bm\bm&amp;\bm\bm
      \bm0.4 &amp;\bm\bm&amp;\bm\bm&amp;\bm\bm
    \end{tabular}</p>
        <p>Verify that <m>v(t)=4.9-4.9e^{-2t}</m> is the solution to the initial
  value problem given by this differential equation and the initial
  condition <m>v(0)=0</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Compare your estimate of <m>v(0.4)</m> to the exact value of <m>v(0.4)</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Convert the following statements into differential equations.</p>
        <p>\begin{itemize}
  \item ``The rate of change of the balance of the account equals 6% of
    the balance.''  Write this as a differential equation for the
    balance <m>B(t)</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>\item ``The population of a town is decreasing at the rate of 2%
    per year.''  Write this as a differential equation for the
    population <m>P(t)</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>\item ``You have a mortgage that grows by 5% every year at the same
    time that you are decreasing it by paying $10,000 per year.''
    Write this as a differential equation for <m>M(t)</m>, the balance of
    the mortgage.
  \end{itemize}</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
